cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use biomed-mcp-receipts, please cite it as below."
title: "biomed-mcp-receipts: checking biomedical MCP servers against primary sources"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hemedan
    given-names: Ahmed
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-07
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/a7med7emedan/biomed-mcp-receipts"
keywords:
  - model context protocol
  - benchmark
  - biomedical data
  - provenance
  - RO-Crate
  - clinical trials
  - PubMed
abstract: >-
  biomed-mcp-receipts calls the tools of biomedical Model Context Protocol servers directly, asks the
  primary source the same question during the same run, and scores the two answers on seven
  dimensions: conformance, schema, correctness, freshness, attribution, robustness and stability.
  Every check is written as a hash-chained receipt, and each run is described as an RO-Crate.
